      "text": [
        "3456 - سَأَلَ إِسْحَاقُ بْنُ عَمَّارٍ أَبَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ :\nعَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ يُعْتِقُ مَمْلُوكَهُ عَنْ دُبُرٍ ثُمَّ يَحْتَاجُ إِلَى ثَمَنِهِ قَالَ \"يَبِيعُهُ\" قَالَ قُلْتُ فَإِنْ كَانَ لَهُ عَنْ ثَمَنِهِ غِنًى قَالَ \"إِذَا رَضِيَ اَلْمَمْلُوكُ فَلاَ بَأْسَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3456 - Ishaq ibn Ammar asked Abu Ibrahim (Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim) (as), about a man who frees his slave as a delayed emancipation (to take effect after his death) and then becomes in need of the slave's price.\nImam (as) said: \"He may sell him.\"\nI asked: \"What if he is not in need of the price?\"\nImam (as) said: \"If the slave agrees, then there is no harm.\""
        ]
      }
    },
